  "serviceLinesNote": "A rule is a list of entries. Each entry is one treatment with the service lines it applies to and the relationships it applies to (measured from an audit client). Relationships are always listed explicitly. Service lines are either listed explicitly, by value from the serviceLines catalog below, or set to [\"default\"]. A default entry applies to its relationships for any service line that no explicit entry in the same rule names for that relationship, so it means anything not mentioned. Each combination of relationship and service line must resolve to exactly one treatment in a rule: an explicit entry beats a default entry, the same relationship and service line cannot appear in two explicit entries, and a relationship can appear in at most one default entry. A treatment may appear in as many entries as needed. A relationship with no matching entry is out of scope. The wizard does not ask for a service line yet.",

